-- keys.lem: a rule that reads a relation through its key
-- (src/lem/eval.rs). UsesK's K(k, _) has `_`, and B binds its `k`; K's key
-- is `k`, so it matches one fact at most, and a change to K is followed.
-- While K's key doesn't hold, K(k, _) matches more, and a tick fails; the
-- next runs every rule whole, so that what UsesK counted then doesn't stay.
input B(n: Int)
input C(n: Int)
rel K(k: Int, n: Int) key k
K(0, n) :- C(n)
rel UsesK(k: Int)
UsesK(k) :- B(k), K(k, _)
-- Q's P(n, _, _) has `_` in a column of P's key, so it may match more than
-- one fact: a change to P runs Q's rule whole. After the tick that fails,
-- the next runs it whole, as two of P's facts match.
input P(a: Int, b: Int, c: Int) key a, b
rel Q(n: Int)
Q(n) :- B(n), P(n, _, _)
